A||||15||ounmongk||I've caught the need for speed disease.||||1||
Z||000000||ounmongk||01-11-2000||05:58 PM||||hey guys, <BR>A ford ecsort tried to race me today, sorry to say, he kept up with me rather well. I really don't want this to happen again though. I was wondering if the performance upgrade from the fiero store is a good investment. Also, I was wondering if there are any other tips you can offer to someone on a budget. ( I still have to go to school, oyu know) My car, an 87 4cyl SE, is all stock, I've done nothing to the engine yet, except for a tune-up. any suggestions would be greatly appreciated, thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||01-11-2000||08:17 PM||||I raced my brother’s 90-ford escort with my 87 coupe that had a 4 cylinder and an automatic trans. I just barely beat him by a car length. There's not much you can do to an Iron Duke.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ounmongk||01-11-2000||08:30 PM||||Iron Duck is more like it, I guess. Quack. are you sure? I've seen 4cyl integras run a quarter mile in 16 some-odd seconds. Crx's even!  is there really no hope for the four banger??? ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ed||01-11-2000||08:45 PM||||The cure for 4's is a 6! I had a four for several years. I was going up a mountain pass here in California when I got passed by a non-turbo Starion. I knew for sure at that point I wanted a six. When my 84 (bought new in January '84) got rear-ended and totalled, that was my opportunity to get a GT. (Although I think the four handles better 'cause its lighter).    ||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||01-11-2000||11:47 PM||||Isn't anybody gonna help this dude? Ok, give summit racing a call and they can hook you up with a Holly TBI unit that flows MUCH better than the stock one.  It will cost you in the neighborhood of 300 bucks though, so be warned.  A good tune-up including timing check, plugs, wires, cap, rotor, and air filter should be a benefit.  A K&N filter wouldn't hurt, but wouldn't gain you much either.  If it's an automatic, you could check out a shift kit from the Fiero Store too.  Am I missing anything?  Oh yeah, supposedly, summit can get their hands on a header for the Fiero too, but I don't know anybody that's tried to get one. <P>later..||||reg||1
Z||000005||2FAST4U||01-12-2000||12:46 AM||||Hooker makes the header. I have one and I believe Sloponti has one also. It works great and you can get it from just about any speed shop. To get the most from the header you will need a better exhauste system. I used 2 1/2" tubing, a Dynomax muffler and a larger catalytic converter.You also might remove the restriction in the side air intake. Better ignition coil (MSD) makes a big difference too. These mods and the ones mentioned in the earlier replies are about all that can be done without getting into the engine. <p>[This message has been edited by 2FAST4U (edited 01-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||ounmongk||01-12-2000||01:52 AM||||2fast, what do you mean by the restriction in the side air intake? can I do this myself?<BR>Also, should I look into performance chip upgrade? Anything I should do for cooling?||||reg||1
Z||000007||mrfiero||01-12-2000||02:02 AM||||GT Bastard,<P>The bigger Holley TBI will not work on '87 or '88 coupes.....just the '84-'86, so his options are even more limited.<P>    ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Patrick||01-12-2000||03:13 AM||||<BR>There is no performance chip upgrade for the 2.5L engine.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Carrolles||01-12-2000||06:34 AM||||The 4 cylinder engines in todays cars are much better than the early eighty's vintage Iron Duke.  I've been renting a 99 Mercury Mystique for this latest field assignment.  I knew it was a 4 banger by the lack of low end torque but was surprised to find that it is a 2.0L engine.  It is quite peppy for a medium sized car.<P>Most of today's 4 bangers have overhead cams (some have several) and multi valves and far better fuel management systems than our cars came with.||||reg||1
Z||000010||ChadMan||01-12-2000||09:32 AM||||Sadly, there aren't many "bolt-on" mods for the Duck that are worth a darn.  Your 87 already has the high-flow intake and TBI (98 hp v. 92).  Going with a header and free-flow cat might get you up around 105 hp, but unless you want to go with an SD-4, turbocharging, or nitrous, that's as good as it's gonna get!<P>The last generation Dukes (as found in Cieras, Calais, etc in the early 90s) were rated for 110 hp at 5200 rpm.  Note the 12 hp boost, and that the hp peak comes 200 rpm higher than the redline on our Fiero Dukes.  I have never been able to find out what the improvements were, but if my Duke ever blows up and I decide to replace it with another, I'll check into the newer Dukes.  Hey, 12 hp is 12 hp. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||WGraffiKs||01-11-2000||04:24 PM||||Chad,<BR>What's an SD-4?  What are it's applications (will it work on a V6?)and what is the price/availability?<BR>Sorry so many questions, but hey, YOU brought it up!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000012||ounmongk||01-11-2000||05:42 PM||||hmm. maybe I can save up for a nitrous system, maybe even a turbocharger. How much of a shot can this tired old engine take? How much of a boost can it take? My friend blew up his custom engine at the track when he shot it too long. seems a piston broke under the pressure and that, in turn, tore up the inside of the engine. That was a newly machined engine though. Can my Iron Duck handle this quacktastic power?||||reg||1
Z||000013||Steven||01-11-2000||05:43 PM||||No it will not work on a 6cyl. The reason is the sd-4 is a Super Duty 4 Cylinder. It makes a lot of power, but you will have to pay a LOT of money to get one. Check some of the other threads, because I know that I did read about someone finding a company that had them, and was sell them.  ||||reg||1
Z||000014||ChadMan||01-12-2000||10:20 AM||||The SD-4 (Super Duty) was Pontiac Motorsports' racing version of the Iron Duke, and it was capable of up to 330 hp.  It shared very few parts with the stock Duke and featured a highly modified block and unique cylinder head.<P>There are still sources of performance parts for the Duke (such as Accelerated Motion - check out their Duke page at <A HREF="http://www.amotion.com/p4.html)." TARGET=_blank>www.amotion.com/p4.html).</A>   But getting serious power from the Iron Duke requires a total rebuild with new internal parts, and that means $$$.||||reg||1
Z||000015||ChadMan||01-12-2000||10:24 AM||||Crap - I somehow included a parenthesis and period in the URL.  Try this:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.amotion.com/p4.html" TARGET=_blank>www.amotion.com/p4.html</A> ||||reg||1
